module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.AdicQuotientComparisonPinned
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.ClosureProductsAndFibres
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.StrictAdicMilnorFibre
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Cohomology.DerivedLimit.MilnorFibreKInjective
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Cohomology.Slice.DerivedIsomorphismLocality

/-!
# Part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0A0K] reduced to the invertibility of one named map

Let `(𝒞, 𝒪)` be a ringed site, `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪` a sheaf of ideals and `K ↦ K^∧` a derived completion
functor. Part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0A0K] asserts

`K^∧ = R lim (K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 𝒪/ℐⁿ)`

for an **arbitrary** object `K` of `D(𝒪)`. This file reduces it to `IsIso` of a single map given by
a formula, so that it can be checked on a cover.

## The three named pieces

Write `K = Q K̃` for a K-flat complex `K̃` — every object of `D(𝒪)` is one
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.exists_kFlat_representative`, [Stacks, Tag 06YS]).

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.kInjectiveAdicMilnorObj` is the strict Milnor fibre of the
  **levelwise K-injective replacement** of the strictified tower `n ↦ Tot(K̃ ⊗_𝒪 (𝒪/ℐⁿ⁺¹)[0])`,
  read in `D(𝒪)`. By `Stacks.MilnorTower.isDerivedLimit_Q_kInjectiveMilnorObj` it is a derived
  limit of the tower **with no exactness of countable products assumed** — Grothendieck's axiom
  AB4\*, which fails for sheaves of modules on a site, is replaced by [Stacks, Tag 0BK6]. This is
  what makes a *named* `R lim` available here at all; the fibre of the unreplaced tower,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.strictAdicMilnorFibre`, is a derived limit only under AB4\*.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.kInjectiveAdicComparison` is the map `K ⟶ R lim` out of the strict
  cone: the Milnor augmentation map `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.strictAdicComparison` of
  [Stacks, Tag 0CQH] followed by the Milnor fibre of the resolution inclusion. Both factors are
  formulas, so it is one.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.adicMilnorCompletionComparison` is the resulting map
  `c : K^∧ ⟶ R lim`, pinned by the universal property of the completion
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.pinnedAdicComparison`): the target is derived complete, being a
  derived limit of derived-complete objects ([Stacks, Tag 091W]).

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedLimit_kInjectiveAdicMilnorObj` — the named object is a
  derived limit of `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.adicReductionTower`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedComplete_kInjectiveAdicMilnorObj` — and it is derived
  complete.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.kInjectiveAdicComparison_comp_kInjectiveProj` — the composites of
  the comparison map with the named projections are the maps of the strict cone, on the nose; so
  it is the comparison map of [Stacks, Tag 0CQH] and not some other map into some other object.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedLimit_derivedCompletion_adicReductionTower_of_isIso` —
  **part (1) from `IsIso c`.**
* `RingedSite.isDerivedLimit_derivedCompletion_adicReductionTower_of_isIso_of_iso` — the same
  for an arbitrary `K` isomorphic to `Q K̃`, which is every object of `D(𝒪)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedLimit_derivedCompletion_adicReductionTower_of_coversTop`
  — **part (1) reduced to a chart-by-chart statement**, the comparison map being a formula and so
  testable on a family covering the final object of the site.

## What remains, and where the amplitude hypothesis went

What remains is `IsIso c`, and `c` is a formula, so
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isIso_of_coversTop_mapDerivedCategory` applies to it directly: it is enough
to invert the restriction of `c` to the slice over each member of a family covering the final
object. That restriction is the slice's own pinned comparison, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletionRestrictIso_hom_app_comp_map_pinnedAdicComparison`
of `AdicMilnorComparisonSliceRestriction.lean`, so the hypothesis contains no global map.

**No bound on the amplitude of `K` appears in any statement of this file**, and the uniqueness
this file uses is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.hom_ext_derivedCompletionUnit`, for maps *out of*
a derived completion, which is the reflector adjunction and carries no bound. The price paid
instead is that the target must be a formula, which is what the K-flat representative and the
K-injective replacement buy.

**It does not follow that the amplitude hypothesis has been removed from part (1); it has been
moved into the chart hypothesis.** On a chart where `ℐ` is generated by finitely many sections the
derived completion is the Čech completion of [Stacks, Tag 099B] and part (1) is available
(`Stacks.Algebraization.isDerivedLimitWithProjections_adicReductionTower_generatedIdealSheaf`),
and `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_pinnedAdicComparison_of_iso` converts an identification of
the two sides there *compatible with the two maps out of `K`* into `IsIso` of the restriction.
What the chart statement supplies is weaker than that: it says `(K|_V)^∧` and the restricted
`R lim` are both derived limits of the restricted tower and that the pinned comparison matches
their projections (`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.pinnedAdicComparison_comp`), and matching
projections does **not** make a comparison invertible — the third square of the morphism of Milnor
triangles is undetermined, with indeterminacy
`Hom((K|_V)^∧, (∏ₙ K|_V ⊗^𝐋 𝒪_V/(ℐ|_V)ⁿ⁺¹)⟦-1⟧)`. That is precisely the group
`Stacks.Algebraization.hom_ext_of_comp_proj` of
`Completion/AdicQuotientCanonicalComparison.lean` kills from `IsLE 0` on the source and `IsGE 0`
on the terms of the tower, and whose non-vanishing the docstring of
`Stacks.Algebraization.isIso_of_isDerivedLimitWithProjections_of_comp_proj` there records, with a
counterexample, as making the projection-matching statement false in general. So the degree bounds
are still the open input for an arbitrary `K`; pinning the comparison by the universal property
makes `IsIso c` local and canonical, which the lifted comparison was not, but does not discharge
them.

Accordingly the assertion in the module documentation of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FormalGeometry/DerivedCompletionRinged/KoszulAdicAffineSliceDerivedLimit.lean` that part (1) on the slices
cannot be globalized because "there is no canonical map between two objects both presented as
derived limits" does not apply to this route: `K^∧` is not merely *presented* as a derived limit,
it has a universal property, and the derived limit it is compared against is named here rather
than produced by `distinguished_cocone_triangle₁`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 06YS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06YS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 091W](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/091W)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0K)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BK6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BK6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CQH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CQH)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard
attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.hasSheafCompose_forget₂_ringCat

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u})
  (I : SheafOfModules.Submodule
    (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))

attribute [local instance]
  hasProductsOfShape_nat_derivedCategory_ringSheaf_adicQuotientFactorization

/-- **The adic reduction tower is functorial in the object.** An isomorphism `K ≅ K'` of `D(𝒪)`
induces one of the towers `n ↦ K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 𝒪/ℐⁿ⁺¹`, componentwise the image of `K ≅ K'` under the
derived tensor product.

Separated out as a definition because the whiskering is what carries the transport of part (1)
from a K-flat representative to an arbitrary object of `D(𝒪)`. -/
def adicReductionTowerIsoOfIso
    {K K' : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))}
    (e : K ≅ K') : adicReductionTower X I K ≅ adicReductionTower X I K' :=
  NatIso.ofComponents
    (fun n ↦ ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedTensorProductFunctor X).mapIso e).app
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
          (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) 0).obj
        ((adicQuotientTower X I).obj n)))
    fun _ ↦ ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedTensorProductFunctor X).mapIso e).hom.naturality _

variable (Kt : CochainComplex (Modules X) ℤ)

/-! ### The named `R lim` and the named map into it -/

/-- **The named `R lim (K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 𝒪/ℐⁿ⁺¹)`**: the strict Milnor fibre of the levelwise K-injective
replacement of the strictified adic reduction tower, read in `D(𝒪)`.

The replacement is what removes AB4\*. `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.strictAdicMilnorFibre`, the
Milnor fibre of the tower itself, is a derived limit only when `Q(∏ₙ Kₙ)` is the product of
`n ↦ Q Kₙ`, which is exactness of the countable products of the sheaves of modules and false on a
general site; the termwise product of the K-injective terms computes the product with no exactness
([Stacks, Tag 0BK6]). -/
def kInjectiveAdicMilnorObj :
    DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) :=
  DerivedCategory.Q.obj (Stacks.MilnorTower.kInjectiveMilnorObj (Modules X)
    (strictAdicReductionTower X I Kt))

/-- **The named map `K ⟶ R lim (K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 𝒪/ℐⁿ⁺¹)`**: the Milnor augmentation map of the strict
cone of [Stacks, Tag 0CQH], followed by the Milnor fibre of the levelwise resolution inclusion.

Both factors are formulas in `K̃` and `ℐ`, with nothing chosen. That is the whole point: a lift of
the cone through the Milnor triangle is determined only up to `Hom(K, (∏ₙ Kₙ)⟦-1⟧)`, so a lift says
nothing after restriction to a chart, while this map restricts to the corresponding map of the
chart. -/
def kInjectiveAdicComparison :
    DerivedCategory.Q.obj Kt ⟶ kInjectiveAdicMilnorObj X I Kt :=
  DerivedCategory.Q.map (strictAdicComparison X I Kt ≫
    Stacks.MilnorTower.mappingCoconeMap
      (Stacks.MilnorTower.kInjectiveTowerInclusion (Modules X)
        (strictAdicReductionTower X I Kt)))

/-- **The named comparison map recovers the strict cone**: its composite with the `n`-th named
projection of the K-injective Milnor fibre is the image of the `n`-th map of the strict cone of
[Stacks, Tag 0CQH].

This is what says the map of this file is the comparison map of that tag and not some other map:
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.Q_strictAdicAugmentationApp` identifies the right-hand side, through
the K-flat comparison, with the derived reduction `K ⟶ K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 𝒪/ℐⁿ⁺¹`.

The projections of the replacement land in the terms of the replacement tower and
`Stacks.MilnorTower.kInjectiveProj` corrects them by the inverse of the resolution inclusion; the
correction cancels the inclusion that `Stacks.MilnorTower.mappingCoconeMap_proj` produces, which is
why no hypothesis on `K̃` is needed. -/
theorem kInjectiveAdicComparison_comp_kInjectiveProj (n : ℕ) :
    kInjectiveAdicComparison X I Kt ≫ Stacks.MilnorTower.kInjectiveProj (Modules X)
        (strictAdicReductionTower X I Kt) n =
      DerivedCategory.Q.map (strictAdicAugmentationApp X I Kt n) := by
  have hstrict : (strictAdicComparison X I Kt ≫
        Stacks.MilnorTower.mappingCoconeMap
          (Stacks.MilnorTower.kInjectiveTowerInclusion (Modules X)
            (strictAdicReductionTower X I Kt))) ≫
        Stacks.MilnorTower.proj (Stacks.MilnorTower.kInjectiveTower (Modules X)
          (strictAdicReductionTower X I Kt)) n =
      strictAdicAugmentationApp X I Kt n ≫
        (Stacks.MilnorTower.kInjectiveTowerInclusion (Modules X)
          (strictAdicReductionTower X I Kt)).app ⟨n⟩ := by
    rw [Category.assoc, Stacks.MilnorTower.mappingCoconeMap_proj, ← Category.assoc,
      strictAdicComparison_proj]
  have hcancel : DerivedCategory.Q.map
        ((Stacks.MilnorTower.kInjectiveTowerInclusion (Modules X)
          (strictAdicReductionTower X I Kt)).app ⟨n⟩) ≫
      (Stacks.MilnorTower.kInjectiveTowerIso (Modules X)
        (strictAdicReductionTower X I Kt)).inv.app ⟨n⟩ = 𝟙 _ :=
    Iso.hom_inv_id_app
      (Stacks.MilnorTower.kInjectiveTowerIso (Modules X)
        (strictAdicReductionTower X I Kt)) ⟨n⟩
  calc DerivedCategory.Q.map (strictAdicComparison X I Kt ≫
          Stacks.MilnorTower.mappingCoconeMap
            (Stacks.MilnorTower.kInjectiveTowerInclusion (Modules X)
              (strictAdicReductionTower X I Kt))) ≫
        (DerivedCategory.Q.map (Stacks.MilnorTower.proj
            (Stacks.MilnorTower.kInjectiveTower (Modules X)
              (strictAdicReductionTower X I Kt)) n) ≫
          (Stacks.MilnorTower.kInjectiveTowerIso (Modules X)
            (strictAdicReductionTower X I Kt)).inv.app ⟨n⟩)
      = DerivedCategory.Q.map (strictAdicAugmentationApp X I Kt n) ≫
          (DerivedCategory.Q.map ((Stacks.MilnorTower.kInjectiveTowerInclusion (Modules X)
              (strictAdicReductionTower X I Kt)).app ⟨n⟩) ≫
            (Stacks.MilnorTower.kInjectiveTowerIso (Modules X)
              (strictAdicReductionTower X I Kt)).inv.app ⟨n⟩) := by
        rw [← Category.assoc, ← Category.assoc, ← DerivedCategory.Q.map_comp,
          ← DerivedCategory.Q.map_comp, hstrict]
    _ = DerivedCategory.Q.map (strictAdicAugmentationApp X I Kt n) ≫ 𝟙 _ := by
        rw [hcancel]
    _ = DerivedCategory.Q.map (strictAdicAugmentationApp X I Kt n) := Category.comp_id _

/-! ### It is a derived limit, and it is derived complete -/

/-- **The named object is a derived limit of the adic reduction tower**, with no exactness of
countable products assumed.

`Stacks.MilnorTower.isDerivedLimit_Q_kInjectiveMilnorObj` gives it for the strictified tower, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.strictAdicReductionTowerIso` identifies that tower with
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.adicReductionTower` at `Q K̃` for `K̃` K-flat. -/
theorem isDerivedLimit_kInjectiveAdicMilnorObj
    (hKt : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsKFlat X.O Kt) :
    IsDerivedLimit (adicReductionTower X I (DerivedCategory.Q.obj Kt))
      (kInjectiveAdicMilnorObj X I Kt) :=
  IsDerivedLimit.of_natIso (strictAdicReductionTowerIso X I Kt hKt).symm
    (Stacks.MilnorTower.isDerivedLimit_Q_kInjectiveMilnorObj (Modules X)
      (strictAdicReductionTower X I Kt))

/-- **The named object is derived complete.** It is a derived limit of a tower of derived-complete
objects — each term `K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 𝒪/ℐⁿ⁺¹` is derived complete by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedComplete_derivedTensor_adicQuotient` — so [Stacks, Tag 091W]
in the form `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedComplete_of_isDerivedLimit` applies. This is
what lets the comparison out of `K^∧` be pinned by the universal property of the completion. -/
theorem isDerivedComplete_kInjectiveAdicMilnorObj
    (hKt : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsKFlat X.O Kt) :
    IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X I (kInjectiveAdicMilnorObj X I Kt) :=
  isDerivedComplete_of_isDerivedLimit X I _ _
    (isDerivedLimit_kInjectiveAdicMilnorObj X I Kt hKt)
    fun n ↦ isDerivedComplete_derivedTensor_adicQuotient X I
      (DerivedCategory.Q.obj Kt) (n + 1)

/-! ### The pinned comparison, and part (1) -/

variable [(ObjectProperty.ι (IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X I)).IsRightAdjoint]

/-- **The comparison map `K^∧ ⟶ R lim (K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 𝒪/ℐⁿ⁺¹)` of part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0A0K], given
by a formula.**

It is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.kInjectiveAdicComparison` factored through the completion unit,
which the universal property of the derived completion does uniquely because the target is derived
complete. Nothing is chosen, so its restriction to a slice site is the corresponding map there and
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isIso_of_coversTop_mapDerivedCategory` applies to it. -/
def adicMilnorCompletionComparison (hKt : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsKFlat X.O Kt) :
    (derivedCompletion X I).obj (DerivedCategory.Q.obj Kt) ⟶ kInjectiveAdicMilnorObj X I Kt :=
  pinnedAdicComparison X I (isDerivedComplete_kInjectiveAdicMilnorObj X I Kt hKt)
    (kInjectiveAdicComparison X I Kt)

/-- The defining property of `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.adicMilnorCompletionComparison`:
composing the completion unit with it gives the named map out of `K`. -/
theorem derivedCompletionUnit_comp_adicMilnorCompletionComparison
    (hKt : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsKFlat X.O Kt) :
    (derivedCompletionUnit X I).app (DerivedCategory.Q.obj Kt) ≫
        adicMilnorCompletionComparison X I Kt hKt =
      kInjectiveAdicComparison X I Kt :=
  derivedCompletionUnit_comp_pinnedAdicComparison X I _ _

/-- **Part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0A0K] for `K = Q K̃` with `K̃` K-flat, given that the named
comparison map is invertible.**

Invertibility of that map is the only thing left, and it is local on the site because the map is a
formula. No hypothesis on the amplitude of `K̃` is used — see the module documentation. -/
theorem isDerivedLimit_derivedCompletion_adicReductionTower_of_isIso
    (hKt : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsKFlat X.O Kt)
    (hc : IsIso (adicMilnorCompletionComparison X I Kt hKt)) :
    IsDerivedLimit (adicReductionTower X I (DerivedCategory.Q.obj Kt))
      ((derivedCompletion X I).obj (DerivedCategory.Q.obj Kt)) :=
  isDerivedLimit_derivedCompletion_of_isIso_pinnedAdicComparison X I
    (isDerivedComplete_kInjectiveAdicMilnorObj X I Kt hKt) (kInjectiveAdicComparison X I Kt) _
    (isDerivedLimit_kInjectiveAdicMilnorObj X I Kt hKt) hc

/-- **Part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0A0K] for an arbitrary object of `D(𝒪)`, given that the named
comparison map of one of its K-flat representatives is invertible.**

Every object of `D(𝒪)` is isomorphic to `Q K̃` for a K-flat `K̃`
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.exists_kFlat_representative`, [Stacks, Tag 06YS]), so this is part
(1) at the full generality of the source, reduced to `IsIso` of a map given by a formula.

The transport is along the isomorphism in both arguments at once: the tower depends on `K` through
the functor `K ↦ K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 -`, and the completion through `K ↦ K^∧`. -/
theorem isDerivedLimit_derivedCompletion_adicReductionTower_of_isIso_of_iso
    (hKt : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsKFlat X.O Kt)
    {K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))}
    (e : DerivedCategory.Q.obj Kt ≅ K)
    (hc : IsIso (adicMilnorCompletionComparison X I Kt hKt)) :
    IsDerivedLimit (adicReductionTower X I K) ((derivedCompletion X I).obj K) :=
  IsDerivedLimit.of_isoObj ((derivedCompletion X I).mapIso e)
    (IsDerivedLimit.of_natIso (adicReductionTowerIsoOfIso X I e)
      (isDerivedLimit_derivedCompletion_adicReductionTower_of_isIso X I Kt hKt hc))

/-! ### Part (1) reduced to a chart-by-chart statement -/

section Locality

variable [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [HasSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [HasWeakSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ V : X.C, HasWeakSheafify (X.J.over V) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ V : X.C, (X.J.over V).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ V : X.C, HasSheafify (X.J.over V) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]

/-- **Part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0A0K] for an arbitrary object of `D(𝒪)`, reduced to a
chart-by-chart statement about one named map.**

Let `V : ι → 𝒞` be a family covering the final object of the site. If the restriction of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.adicMilnorCompletionComparison` to the slice over each `V i` is
invertible, then the derived completion of `K` is a derived limit of the tower
`n ↦ K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 𝒪/ℐⁿ⁺¹`.

This is the precise boundary this route reaches. What is being restricted is a formula, so
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isIso_of_coversTop_mapDerivedCategory` applies to it with nothing further
assumed; the earlier route had only a lift of a cone through a Milnor triangle, which is
determined up to `Hom(K^∧, (∏ₙ Tₙ)⟦-1⟧)` and therefore says nothing after restriction.

**The hypothesis is not literally an amplitude condition, but it is where one is still needed.**
No `IsLE`/`IsGE` bound on `K` is used in reaching this statement, in contrast to the route that
inverts a comparison by a uniqueness statement for maps *into* a derived limit. Discharging the
hypothesis is another matter. Its restriction-free form is
`RingedSite.isDerivedLimit_derivedCompletion_adicReductionTower_of_coversTop_slice`
of `AdicMilnorComparisonSliceRestriction.lean`, where it reads: on each chart the slice's own
pinned comparison at the restricted named map is invertible. On a chart where `ℐ` is generated by
finitely many sections, `K^∧` is the Čech completion of [Stacks, Tag 099B] and part (1) is
available there
(`Stacks.Algebraization.isDerivedLimitWithProjections_adicReductionTower_generatedIdealSheaf`),
and `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_pinnedAdicComparison_of_iso` would convert an
identification of the two sides of the chart *compatible with the two maps out of `K`* into the
hypothesis here — but that chart statement does not supply such an identification. It supplies
two derived-limit presentations of one tower whose projections the comparison matches, and that
is not enough: see the module documentation for the indeterminacy
`Hom((K|_V)^∧, (∏ₙ K|_V ⊗^𝐋 𝒪_V/(ℐ|_V)ⁿ⁺¹)⟦-1⟧)` and for
`Stacks.Algebraization.isIso_of_isDerivedLimitWithProjections_of_comp_proj`, which is the library's
record that the degree bounds are what kills it.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached: this is a conditional statement and proves no assertion of
the tag. Part (1) is registered, under the stronger hypotheses of a quasi-compact scheme and an
ideal generated by global sections, at
`Stacks.Algebraization.isDerivedLimit_derivedTensor_adicQuotientSystem_completion`. -/
theorem isDerivedLimit_derivedCompletion_adicReductionTower_of_coversTop
    (hKt : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsKFlat X.O Kt)
    {K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))}
    (e : DerivedCategory.Q.obj Kt ≅ K)
    {ι : Type*} {V : ι → X.C} (hV : X.J.CoversTop V)
    (hloc : ∀ i, IsIso ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u}
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) (V i)).mapDerivedCategory.map
        (adicMilnorCompletionComparison X I Kt hKt))) :
    IsDerivedLimit (adicReductionTower X I K) ((derivedCompletion X I).obj K) :=
  isDerivedLimit_derivedCompletion_adicReductionTower_of_isIso_of_iso X I Kt hKt e
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isIso_of_coversTop_mapDerivedCategory hV _ hloc)

end Locality

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

end
